# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# The factory drives the GitHub Copilot CLI (`copilot`). There are no provider
# API keys to set: authenticate once with `copilot login` (or export
# COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN with Copilot access) and every
# agent in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml runs on your Copilot plan.
#
# Every `model:` in the config is a bare Copilot model id (e.g. claude-sonnet-5.5,
# gpt-5.6-terra). Which ids you may use depends on your plan; `agents.validate()`
# checks the shape only, so an unavailable model fails when that agent runs.
#
# Spend is reported in premium requests, not dollars.

# Optional overrides
# COPILOT_PATH=copilot             # copilot binary if not on PATH
# COPILOT_HOME=~/.copilot          # where copilot keeps its session logs
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
